3	2	Financial situation (page 3)	Free assets are the assets not tied to liabilities or planned expenses and available at any time; they represent the ability to absorb losses (loss capacity). Free asset ratio = free assets / net liquid assets. Example: liquid assets 5,000,000 less current liabilities 1,000,000 = net liquid assets 4,000,000; less planned expenses 400,000 = free assets 3,600,000; free asset ratio 90%. If 2,000,000 is held with the bank, loss capacity there = 2,000,000 x 90% = 1,800,000.	[0.0611099,0.0715693,-0.168173,-0.0361501,-0.00837859,-0.00754834,0.0540762,-0.0285743,0.023885,0.0183258,0.00821136,0.00288386,0.0622584,-0.00349419,0.057076,0.0316919,-0.0148938,-0.0285741,0.0175395,0.0337327,-0.0169976,-0.0827912,-0.0449331,-0.0121831,0.0011062,0.00689092,-0.00554571,-0.0249592,-0.057713,-0.0111092,-0.0318397,0.00273922,0.0694069,-0.041372,-0.068833,-0.0448395,0.0744146,0.0627864,0.0361369,-0.0254469,-0.0111889,0.0325521,-0.0141637,0.0270524,0.014713,0.0657471,0.0557077,-0.0012009,0.0377284,-0.0349398,0.0763182,0.0226949,-0.0542464,-0.00289074,0.0479007,0.0141255,0.0112813,0.0513933,0.0273902,0.0092295,0.0814463,0.021671,-0.0327674,0.030014,0.0746418,-0.0194283,-0.00532871,0.023205,0.0317844,-0.0360844,0.0267017,0.0382075,-0.0166316,-0.00170094,-0.0436414,-0.01789,-0.0457943,0.032949,0.0157978,-0.0007508,0.0436872,-0.0139034,0.0723359,0.0069856,0.0706676,0.0119973,-0.0127138,-0.0116971,0.0113622,0.0905429,0.058712,0.0285608,0.084741,0.0428264,-0.0436158,0.0389333,-0.00402975,0.0253369,-0.029135,-0.031536,-0.0201337,-0.0040652,0.0426283,-0.0253325,0.022344,0.015294,0.00552227,0.0440057,-0.0418179,0.0155167,0.0178223,0.0331381,-0.023276,0.00636679,-0.0132348,-0.0139631,0.110088,-0.0204832,0.0163586,0.0387041,-0.0173152,0.0116994,0.0839544,0.0216337,0.0176766,0.0256943,-0.0181544,0.0128982,0.0185663,-0.00182966,-0.00676106,-0.0134909,-0.0300019,-0.00828608,0.0177906,0.107761,-0.00273752,-0.0396137,0.010715,0.0481116,0.0577493,-0.011717,-0.00566212,-0.0