9	8	Assessment of the Investor Profile (page 8)	Risk budget = investment amount x maximum historical drawdown of the chosen strategy. Example: 1,000,000 in C-Moderate (25% drawdown) = risk budget 250,000. Total risk budget is the sum across portfolios (conservative: all assets assumed to fall together). Lombard loans raise investment risk and the risk budget. Assessment result: as long as the risk budget is below the loss capacity, the risk taken is in line with the financial situation. Investment horizon: the horizon of each portfolio must be at least the longest historical drawdown of its strategy so there is time to recover.	[0.0776819,0.0593323,-0.180381,0.0122425,0.0360954,-0.0220179,0.0801681,0.0198223,0.0622626,0.0252562,-0.0251501,-0.0280779,0.0570654,-0.00226119,0.0543636,-0.0249726,-0.0170798,-0.0656077,0.0432983,0.0407092,-0.0424622,-0.0565184,-0.0629774,0.0236145,0.011386,0.0190201,-0.0176993,-0.00835773,-0.0449711,0.00725984,0.0118884,0.0153976,-0.00171304,-0.03899,-0.0296978,-0.0518568,0.060968,0.0591469,0.0344894,-0.078865,-0.0337303,0.0231736,0.0422965,-0.0224327,0.0504033,0.0431274,0.0440837,-0.0123672,0.0384108,-0.0111125,0.0355891,-0.00120707,0.0128452,0.0273491,0.0320419,-0.011882,-0.0260046,0.0337316,0.0335617,-0.0375769,0.0704807,0.0143173,-0.0235963,0.0154425,0.0398045,-0.0410792,-0.0521401,0.025679,0.0181149,-0.0212426,0.0277313,0.0164618,-0.00439914,-0.0184202,-0.0487952,0.0546804,-0.00292786,-0.0381511,0.0129346,0.0235546,0.0192694,-0.035028,0.0605144,0.0189155,0.0683918,0.0342344,-0.00101356,0.029539,-0.012412,0.111258,-0.0282432,0.00743575,0.0582777,0.0726633,-0.0768778,0.0469081,-0.0804689,0.0222332,-0.0302407,-0.0035723,-0.00214233,-0.021732,0.0294614,-0.0183814,-0.00703354,0.029511,0.00591992,-0.0164449,-0.0123386,0.0161699,-0.0458778,0.020226,-0.0420887,-0.0357528,-0.00815314,0.000208668,0.0761642,0.0140579,-0.024882,0.0739817,-0.0404704,0.00535454,0.0527384,0.0346462,-0.00347415,0.0720831,-0.0456492,0.0285803,0.0648731,-0.0213555,0.0