jft	1	Draft	2026-10-27	AI draft	AI-generated draft from meeting notes	[{"body": "Return Requirements: The client targets for the portfolio to reach 700M within 8 years.\\nInvestment Time Horizon: The client is a long-term investor, stating the investment period is at least ten years.\\nPrimary Goals: Keeping capital safe comes first for the client.; They want the portfolio to reach 700M within 8 years\\nSecondary Goals: Steady income is second, followed by modest long-term capital growth without an aggressive approach.\\nLiquidity Needs: Not yet completed\\nTax Considerations: Not yet completed\\nUnique Circumstances and Preferences: Not yet completed", "part": 1, "owner": "rm", "title": "Client goals and objectives", "status": "filled"}, {"body": "Liquidity: Strategy B (Income). The client has a risk score of 2 out of 5 (Conservative), and near-term cash needs are held in the lowest-risk strategies (A or B only). Strategy B (Income) has an expected return of about 3.0%, a maximum historical drawdown of 15% and a longest drawdown of 4 years. This portfolio recommendation is designed to generate an average, expected rate of return of 0.5%–1.5% above inflation, net of fees and costs. Based on current projections, this equates to a current nominal return of 2.5%–3.5%. Longevity: Strategy C (Yield). The client has a risk score of 2 out of 5 (Conservative), and this portfolio funds the client's long-term lifestyle and should match risk willingness and capacity. Strategy C (Yield) has an expected return of about 3.5%, a maximum historical drawdown of 25% and a longest drawdown of 4 years. This portfolio recommendation is designed to generate an average, expected rate of return of 1.0%–2.0% above inflation, net of fees and costs. Based on current projections, this equates to a current nominal return of 3.0%–4.0%. Legacy: Strategy D (Balanced). The client has a risk score of 2 out of 5 (Conservative), and this portfolio has the longest horizon, so it can carry a little more risk than Longevity. Strategy D (Balanced) has an expected return of about 4.5%, a maximum historical drawdown of 35% and a longest drawdown of 6 years. This portfolio recommendation is designed to generate an average, expected rate of return of 2.0%–3.0% above inflation, net of fees and costs. Based on current projections, this equates to a current nominal return of 4.0%–5.0%.\\n3L proportion (adds up to 100%): Liquidity 6% (The client has a cash reserve of S$30,000,000 and monthly spending of S$150,000 against managed assets of S$500,000,000, so near-term cash needs take a small share of the portfolio.), Longevity 89% (The client is 45, about 40 years from age 85, with a risk score of 2 out of 5 (Conservative), so most of the portfolio funds the client's long-term lifestyle.), Legacy 5% (No legacy or philanthropy goal is stated, so Legacy stays small for a client aged 45 with a risk score of 2 out of 5 (Conservative).)", "part": 2, "owner": "pm", "title": "3L buckets and explanation", "status": "filled"}, {"body": "Risk tolerance (willingness): The client is very risk averse. A fall of more than 10% in a single year would make her very uncomfortable and likely prompt her to sell; Risk capacity (ability): She has a long horizon, an income of S$10m that covers her costs, and a large asset base; Time horizon: At least ten years; Liquidity needs: She spends about S$150,000 a month on living costs. She wishes to keep a cash reserve of S$30m A fall of more than 10% in a single year would make her very uncomfortable and would likely prompt her to sell", "part": 3, "owner": "rm", "title": "Client risk profile", "status": "filled"}, {"body": "", "part": 4, "owner": "pm", "title": "Strategic Asset Allocation", "status": "empty"}, {"body": "Review frequency: The IPS is reviewed at least annually, and the portfolio is monitored against it on an ongoing basis. Review triggers: An ad-hoc review is held on a material change in the client's circumstances (income, wealth, health, family, liabilities), on a major life event (for example retirement, a property purchase or a child starting university), on a significant market event, when the portfolio deviates from the Strategic Asset Allocation beyond the agreed tolerance bands, or on a regulatory change that affects the mandate. Who reviews: The Relationship Manager leads the review with the client; the Portfolio Manager confirms the allocation and the strategies; compliance sign-off is required for any change to the IPS. Documentation: Every review and every change is recorded as a new IPS version with its date, author, the reason for the change and the supporting meeting note. Communication to the client: The client receives the updated IPS after each review, and is told promptly of any breach of the tolerance bands or any change to the strategy; the client confirms it in writing.", "part": 5, "owner": "rm", "title": "Review rules", "status": "filled"}, {"body": "Signed by the RM on 2026-10-27.", "part": 6, "owner": "rm", "title": "Signature line", "status": "filled"}, {"body": "Approach: safety and steady income; Believes: blue-chip equities, high-grade bonds, government bonds, and companies using ESG screening; Avoids: tobacco, thermal coal, and trading for tax reasons; Investment period: at least ten years", "part": 7, "owner": "rm", "title": "Investment philosophy", "status": "filled"}, {"body": "Employment / income source: Salary; Annual income: S$10m; Date of birth / age: Born on 14 March 1981; Occupation: Chief Executive Officer of CityBank; AUM: S$500m", "part": 8, "owner": "rm", "title": "Demographics", "status": "filled"}]	{"risk": {"fields": {"Time horizon": "At least ten years", "Liquidity needs": "She spends about S$150,000 a month on living costs. She wishes to keep a cash reserve of S$30m", "Risk capacity (ability)": "She has a long horizon, an income of S$10m that covers her costs, and a large asset base", "Risk tolerance (willingness)": "The client is very risk averse. A f