52	note_jft_1020	jft	4	Isabel: Let's talk about cash needs. What do you spend each month? Jane: I spend about S$150,000 a month on living costs, and my salary covers it. I take no regular withdrawals from the portfolio. I would like to keep a cash reserve of S$30m so that I never have to sell investments to meet my expenses, whether that is an emergency or a large one-off bill in a year when markets are down.	[0.0188764,0.048365,-0.168676,0.0238279,-0.060195,0.00458657,0.0380625,-0.0382144,0.1086,0.0261508,-0.0508277,-0.0184673,0.0299864,0.010144,0.0224837,0.0243216,-0.0378634,-0.0509082,0.0455545,0.0601922,-0.0600124,-0.0743835,-0.0520193,0.00871464,0.000552058,0.0182494,-0.0152334,0.00856175,-0.00543837,0.0414287,0.0129522,-0.0176522,0.0225266,-0.038067,-0.0548482,-0.0318735,0.0535459,0.0598284,0.0157501,-0.065218,0.0379458,-0.0343216,0.0454472,-0.0276883,0.0768342,0.043214,0.0606892,-0.0222396,0.0895571,-0.00631122,0.0318398,-0.00507293,-0.0394486,0.0738274,0.0474885,-0.0204195,-0.039247,0.017126,-0.0120781,-0.05103,0.159742,0.00733425,-0.0473414,0.0599921,0.0129832,-0.0159945,-0.0149577,0.00375497,-0.0108096,-0.0411976,0.0418493,-0.000297725,-0.0142726,0.00194143,-0.0567555,0.0730962,-0.0227622,-0.0278815,0.0182719,0.0424145,0.0148559,-0.0530217,0.0691448,-0.0297493,0.0329371,0.0117906,0.0336417,-0.0177345,0.0107674,0.0860648,-0.0112739,0.0385332,0.0485692,0.0602853,-0.00922811,0.0232855,-0.0116077,0.0295457,0.00655692,-0.0241314,-0.0255165,-0.0395572,-0.000175677,0.00257238,0.0419909,0.0306824,-0.0235965,0.00460572,-0.000587359,-0.0251568,-0.0322411,0.0126164,-0.00818382,-0.0466598,-0.0259765,-0.0154009,0.0431897,-0.0348266,0.0088143,0.0684751,-0.0487567,-0.0122512,0.102802,0.0069833,-0.0219579,0.042626,0.00624662,-0.00161642,0.038359,0.00194522,0.000662338,0.02587,-0.0284548,0.00424651,0.0154109,0.0559391,-0.0267393,-0.0343775,-0.0276856,0.0459602,0.083212,0.0425355,0.0347869,-0.0590497,-0.0591634,-0.0304175,0.0434716,-0.00839406,-0.0374656,0.030062,0.0195425,